 \subsection{Policy Definitions}
 Streaming retains the initialized HBM set and fetches misses without GPU admission. The SwapMoE-style FP16 adapter uses a fixed CPU set and GPU LRU replacement. Fiddler-style computes non-HBM experts on the CPU. Both are local mechanism implementations. Independent caching updates HBM/CPU recency separately; MECC couples GPU promotion to victim demotion. MECC I/O is a separate delivery control.
 
-FlashMoE-RF combines public inverse-recency and frequency features with equal weights, using HBM LRU. Its host score is $0.5/d_e+0.5f_e/f_{\max}$, with request distance $d_e$ and count $f_e$. The lowest score is evicted; ID breaks ties. The original trained predictor is absent. Plot labels abbreviate SwapMoE-style as Swap-style and FlashMoE-RF as Flash-RF. MoE-CORE and MoE-Infinity have no completed run in this repository.
