 \subsection{Timing and Demand Counters}
 TTFT is time to first token; TPOT is time per output token during decode. Accelerator occupancy is GPU count times TPOT, in GPU-s/token. Measured HDD-demand shares aggregate classified accesses across instrumented phases. Prefetched experts are classified by residency at consumption. These shares are separate from physical read/copy byte counters and decode-only demand. The short-window diagnostic compares streaming and MECC routing, logits, gates, and tokens through their shared dispatch; it is not independent full-model equivalence evidence.
